# Incomplete year cleanup before restart

Multi-year runs create one hash folder per year under `domains/<domain>/raw_runs/<sha256>/`. The orchestrator (`classes/Run.py`) **skips any year whose folder already exists**, with no completeness check. A crash mid-year leaves a partial folder that must be deleted or that year will never re-run.

## Active / queued job guard (do this first)

1. Run `qstat -u $USER`. Note jobs in **`R`** (running) vs **`Q`** (queued).
2. **Never delete** a `raw_runs/<hash>` that an **`R`** job is currently writing (last `run_log.txt` line / PBS log for that job).
3. **Queued (`Q`) jobs** that will intentionally recreate a tip year are OK to clean *before* they start — still list paths and get user confirmation.
4. Paths are **per-domain**: `domains/potomac2/raw_runs/<hash>` ≠ `domains/wolf2/raw_runs/<hash>` even when the hash string matches. Delete only the domain you mean (`…/domains/<domain>/raw_runs/<hash>`, not `…/domains/<domain>/<hash>`).

## How to identify the folder to delete

1. **Slurm/PBS logs** in `ensemble_running/` (`*.o<jobid>`): look for `Disk quota exceeded`, `walltime … exceeded`, or other kills. Note the `raw_runs/<hash>` path in the failing I/O line when present.
2. **Confirm with `run_log.txt`**:  
   `domains/<domain>/processed_full_runs/<ensemble>/<member>/run_log.txt`  
   (spinups may nest one more level, e.g. `…/40_year_spinup/spinup/run_log.txt`).  
   The **last** `Running year N of the run in …/raw_runs/<hash>` line is the incomplete **tip** year. If there is no `Finished running full sequence` line, the sequence did not complete.
3. **Sanity-check completeness**:
   - **Tip incomplete (delete):** usually no usable `run.out.00001.nc` / no `processed_output.nc`; job died on this year; **no later year dirs** for this sequence on this domain.
   - **Mid-sequence with `run.out.00001.nc` but missing `processed_output.nc`:** often ParFlow finished and later years already ran — **do not delete** if downstream year dirs exist (they need this year as IC). Condensation can create `processed_output.nc` later.
4. **Before deleting a “wrong but complete” year** (e.g. old pumping formula): confirm hash has **no later-year dirs** on that domain for sequences that use it, or you will strand dependents.
5. **Show the user the exact paths** (and whether each is tip-incomplete vs wrong-rate-complete) **and get confirmation before deleting.**

## What to delete / keep

- **Walltime/quota restart:** delete only the incomplete **tip** year’s `raw_runs/<hash>`.
- **Keep** prior complete years; they are restart ICs.
- **Keep** mid-sequence dirs that have ParFlow output when later years already exist.
- Freeing disk does **not** resume a dead job; restart the sequence after cleanup (and after quota headroom if that was the failure mode).

## Do not rely on

- `file_locations.json` — written after post-processing, not mid-run progress.
- Folder existence — means “started,” not “finished.”
- Hash including computed fluxes — hash is wetness / `pumping_rate_fraction` / irrigation only; fixing pumping math does **not** change the hash (must delete bad years to re-run).
